{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"kimberlite-mindful-nabarlek","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# 9790's field-readiness budget is too short: the DC harness now errors ALL 62 cells at setup\n\n## Status: BREAKS e369's exit bar\n\nEpic [rebar:e369-a449-4773-48fb]'s 14th criterion is \"the live DC harness job is GREEN end to end\n(0 failed cells)\". It is currently RED at `main`, so the bar is not met. This regression was\nintroduced by [rebar:9790-cafa-dffa-462e] (Gerrit 1406, merged), which replaced the harness's\n`serverInfo` readiness gate with a field-registration wait.\n\n## Evidence\n\nHarness run **30975323866** at `31f352d535`: **1 xfailed, 62 ERRORS in 606.98s** — every cell errored\nat fixture setup, none ran. The immediately preceding run **30964805133** at `c3fb869ab5` (before\n1406 landed) was **62 passed, 1 xfailed, 0 failed**.\n\n    RuntimeError: Jira DC at http://localhost:2990/jira: required Epic field(s) Epic Link, Epic Name\n    were still absent after 61 poll(s) over 600s.\n    Last observation: GET /rest/api/2/field -> HTTP 200, 27 field(s); names observed:\n    ['Archived', 'Archiver', 'Attachment', 'Comment', 'Created', 'Creator', 'Images', 'Key',\n     'Last Viewed', 'Log Work', 'Original Estimate', 'Progress', 'Project', 'Remaining Estimate',\n     'Resolved', 'Status', 'Sub-Tasks', 'Time Spent', 'Time Tracking', 'Updated', 'Votes',\n     'Watchers', 'Work Ratio', 'Σ Original Estimate', 'Σ Progress', 'Σ Remaining Estimate',\n     'Σ Time Spent']\n\n## Diagnosis — the message diagnoses itself, which is 9790 AC2 working as designed\n\n9790's `not_ready_message` states the decision rule: *\"if it contains no `customfield_*` entries\nwhatsoever the plugin is still starting and the budget (`JIRA_DC_FIELD_READY_TIMEOUT`) is too short;\nif it contains other custom fields but not these, the image genuinely changed\"*.\n\nThe observed inventory has **ZERO `customfield_*` entries** — all 27 are system fields. So:\n**READINESS/TIMING, not a genuine degrade, and not a name-matching bug.** The GreenHopper plugin had\nnot finished registering within the 600s budget.\n\nThis is the SAME 27-field system-only inventory 9790 itself cited from run 30944211742. The wait is\nbehaving correctly — it correctly refuses a not-ready instance. The budget is simply wrong for this\nimage on this runner.\n\n## Why the old gate \"worked\"\n\nThe `serverInfo` gate let the run proceed immediately, and the tests passed because the fields had\nregistered long before any cell actually needed `Epic Link`. 9790 correctly identified that as a\nlatent flake — but converted it into a HARD failure at a budget shorter than the plugin's real\nregistration time, which is strictly worse for the same instance.\n\n## The gap in 9790's acceptance criteria — worth recording\n\n9790's five criteria were all met and I verified each against the change. **None of them required the\nharness to still pass end to end.** They constrained the readiness DEFINITION, not its effect on the\nrun — exactly the same shape as e369's original 13 criteria being satisfiable while three live cells\nfailed. A criterion set that does not include \"the thing still works\" can be fully met by a change\nthat breaks it.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] the field-readiness budget is sized from MEASURED plugin-registration time on this image, with\n      the measurement recorded (run id + observed delay), not guessed\n- [ ] the harness run is GREEN end to end again (0 failed, 0 errored cells) — proven by a live run,\n      with the run id recorded\n- [ ] the wait still FAILS loudly on a genuine degrade (custom fields present but not the Epic ones),\n      so raising the budget does not re-introduce the blindness 9790 removed — pinned by a test\n- [ ] `JIRA_DC_FIELD_READY_TIMEOUT`'s default and its override path are documented where an operator\n      will find them when a run times out\n\n## Testing\n\n    gh workflow run \"Live External Integration\" --ref main\n    pytest tests/unit/test_live_jira_dc_conftest.py -q","id":"941b-f049-5f29-4410","parent_id":"e369-a449-4773-48fb","priority":1,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"9790's field-readiness budget is too short: the DC harness errors all 62 cells at setup"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785906588570240001,"uuid":"72a21126-45a1-4f97-b17d-8946d42526be"}